; Andree, Programming the IBM 650 (1958), section 3-10, Example 1 (p.55):
; T = (A + B) x C / D for every card of a data deck, punching A, B, C,
; D and T on a result card -- the program exactly as printed.
;
; Data card (formula.cards), all integers:
;   word 1  A  000xxxxxxx       word 3  B  00000xxxxx
;   word 2  C  0000000xxx       word 4  D  00000xxxxx
; Result card: words 1-4 A, B, C, D; word 6 T (the quotient, the
; remainder dropped); word 5 is whatever 1381 holds.
;
; The loop has no exit: with the data used up and End of File pressed,
; the next read finds an empty feed and stops on a read validity check
; -- the usual end of a 650 job. The card cycles (read 300 ms, punch
; 600 ms) hide the drum timing here; see count_*.650 for that.
;
;   l examples/formula.650
;   hopper examples/formula.cards
;   r, eof, r, then punch            (or: deck formula.deck, then
;                                     boot formula.deck examples/formula.cards)

start 0101

0101  RD1  1351 0102    ; read a card into 1351-1360
0102  RAU  1351 0106    ; A
0106  STD  1377 0132    ; store A for punch
0132  AUP  1353 0108    ; A + B
0108  STD  1378 0133    ; store B for punch
0133  MPY  1352 0109    ; (A + B) x C
0109  STD  1379 0134    ; store C for punch
0134  DVR  1354 0110    ; divide by D
0110  STD  1380 0135    ; store D for punch
0135  STL  1382 0139    ; store the result T for punch
0139  WR1  1377 0101    ; punch 1377-1384
